{
    "background_story": "Ailani grew up watching her father work on DIY projects around the house, fascinated by the way he could fix anything with a few tools and some know-how. But it was the plumbing system that really caught her attention - the way water flowed through the pipes, the sound of the toilet flushing, and the satisfaction of fixing a leaky faucet. After completing a vocational program in plumbing, Ailani started her own business, specializing in eco-friendly plumbing solutions. Her company, 'Island Fixers,' quickly gained a reputation for reliable and sustainable services. Ailani took pride in being one of the few female plumbers in the industry, and she loved the sense of independence that came with running her own business. As she often said, 'There's no leak too small, no pipe too clogged, that I won't tackle head-on.'",
